PREDICTIONS -- zakcode arm on the three new tasks          2026-09-12
Written BEFORE the run completes. Claude Code's results are already known
(all three PASS, at 17 / 7 / 8 turns), so these predictions are made with the
reference arm visible -- that is stated plainly rather than hidden, because it
makes the predictions EASIER and they should be discounted accordingly.

WHAT THIS RUN CAN AND CANNOT SHOW (ADR-0151, rb-10756)
  It is MODEL-CONFOUNDED by construction: zakcode runs zds-qwen3.6-35b on the
  pod, Claude Code ran Opus 5. A gap is NOT evidence about the agent loop. What
  a gap DOES establish is that the new tasks have resolving power at all -- if
  zakcode fails where Claude Code passes, these three tasks are the first in the
  suite that separate ANY two arms, which is exactly what ADR-0151 said the
  suite lacks. That is worth having even though it does not answer parity.

PREDICTIONS
  P1  06-plugin-conventions -- FAIL or near-miss. It is the task that cost the
      reference agent the most (2.7x turns), and the cost was EXPLORATION:
      reading CONTRIBUTING.md, noticing the stdlib-only rule, and resisting the
      obvious `import yaml`. A smaller model is most likely to write the obvious
      thing. This is my strongest prediction.
  P2  07-ttl-cache -- roughly even odds. Fully specified, so no exploration is
      needed, and stated intricacy cost the reference agent almost nothing
      (1.1x). But four interacting traps is exactly the shape of 05-ledger's
      atomicity, which is the ONE task zakcode has ever failed.
  P3  08-mutation-leak -- FAIL more likely than pass. Requires tracing a cause
      three modules from its symptom, and the two decoy fixes (silence the
      audit, reload around it) are both more obvious than the root fix.

  Aggregate: I expect 0-1 of 3 to pass.

WHAT EACH OUTCOME MEANS, fixed in advance
  0-2 of 3 pass -> the new tasks DISCRIMINATE. The suite is no longer saturated
      for both arms, ADR-0151's addendum understated the tasks' value, and the
      "stop unsaturating this way" decision must be SOFTENED: the tasks failed
      to separate Claude Code from a ceiling, but they separate the two ARMS,
      which is a different and useful property.
  3 of 3 pass -> the tasks are saturated for both arms exactly like the
      original five, and the decision to stop stands unqualified.
